{
  "rule": "shiki dual-theme highlighting (core/syntax-highlight.ts + the crowiCode sidecar) and its fallback: a supported fence becomes an html node with data.crowiCode {lang, value, tokens} and projects to a code node with data.tokens under X-Crowi-Ast-Version:1; an unsupported / lang-less fence stays a plain code node (lang/meta preserved, nullability per @types/mdast) with no tokens.",
  "why": "Token lines are the ONLY cross-client representation of highlighting (the html node value is a web-only byte string that the v1 projection drops). Both clients must agree on the token line/boundary structure and fontStyle; theme colors are version-dependent styling, not contract.",
  "consumers": [
    "packages/api/src/renderer/golden-corpus.test.ts",
    "apps/apple/CrowiKit/Tests/CrowiKitTests/RenderedAstGoldenCorpusTests.swift"
  ],
  "consumerContract": "The api jest driver asserts the PRODUCER side (markdown → expectedAst via runPipeline with an empty registry, and storedAst/expectedAst → expectedEnvelope via sanitizeAst). The CrowiKit XCTest asserts the CONSUMER side (its sanitize-walker mirror over storedAst/expectedAst, and its strict envelope decoder over expectedEnvelope). The Swift consumer is wired up in Phase 4 (apps/apple lives on the feature-ios-app/impl branch).",
  "normalization": "Shiki theme colors are normalized before comparison: every token style \"color\" / \"bgColor\" value (the \"light\" / \"dark\" objects inside data.tokens) is replaced with the placeholder \"<color>\" on BOTH the expected and the actual tree. Colors are shiki/theme-version-dependent and deliberately not pinned; token line structure, \"content\" boundaries and \"fontStyle\" values ARE pinned verbatim. Highlighted-fence cases omit expectedAst on purpose: the stored side is an html node whose value is a generated byte string (see exclusions) — the pinned artifact is the v1 projection.",
  "exclusions": "Plugin-dispatch output byte strings (Mermaid / PlantUML / link-card / shiki generated HTML) are deliberately NOT pinned by this corpus — packages/e2e/tests/renderer-plugins.spec.ts owns that coverage against a live server. The corpus pins parser/core-transform STRUCTURE and the v1 projection schema shapes only; where a stored html node value would be a generated byte string, the case either omits expectedAst (code.json) or uses a synthetic stand-in value the projection never reads (typed-nodes.json).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "shiki-tokens",
      "why": "the dual-theme token structure: lines of {content, light:{color}, dark:{color}} — light AND dark are both always present (single-color tokens cannot express Crowi’s dark mode)",
      "markdown": "```ts\n// note\nconst x = 1;\n```",
      "expectedEnvelope": {
        "astVersion": 1,
        "root": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "ts",
              "value": "// note\nconst x = 1;",
              "data": {
                "tokens": [
                  [
                    {
                      "content": "// note",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "content": "const",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "content": " ",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "content": "x",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "content": " ",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "content": "=",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "content": " ",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "content": "1",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "content": ";",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "shiki-fontstyle",
      "why": "fontStyle is pinned by real value (bold / italic arrays), unlike colors — it is rendering semantics, not theme styling",
      "markdown": "```markdown\n# Title\n**bold** and _italic_\n```",
      "expectedEnvelope": {
        "astVersion": 1,
        "root": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "markdown",
              "value": "# Title\n**bold** and _italic_",
              "data": {
                "tokens": [
                  [
                    {
                      "content": "# Title",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>",
                        "fontStyle": [
                          "bold"
                        ]
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>",
                        "fontStyle": [
                          "bold"
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  [
                    {
                      "content": "**bold**",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>",
                        "fontStyle": [
                          "bold"
                        ]
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>",
                        "fontStyle": [
                          "bold"
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "content": " and ",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>"
                      }
                    },
                    {
                      "content": "_italic_",
                      "light": {
                        "color": "<color>",
                        "fontStyle": [
                          "italic"
                        ]
                      },
                      "dark": {
                        "color": "<color>",
                        "fontStyle": [
                          "italic"
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "code-unknown-lang",
      "why": "an unknown fence language falls back to a plain code node: lang preserved verbatim, meta null, no html node, no tokens — clients render it plain",
      "markdown": "```zzz-unknown\nplain body\n```",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "zzz-unknown",
            "meta": null,
            "value": "plain body"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expectedEnvelope": {
        "astVersion": 1,
        "root": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "plain body",
              "lang": "zzz-unknown",
              "meta": null
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "code-no-lang",
      "why": "a lang-less fence keeps lang:null (null, not absent — @types/mdast nullability)",
      "markdown": "```\nno lang here\n```",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": null,
            "meta": null,
            "value": "no lang here"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expectedEnvelope": {
        "astVersion": 1,
        "root": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "no lang here",
              "lang": null,
              "meta": null
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "code-meta",
      "why": "code.meta (the fence info string after the lang) is preserved verbatim through both wire shapes",
      "markdown": "```zzz-unknown title=\"x\"\nmeta body\n```",
      "expectedAst": {
        "type": "root",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "zzz-unknown",
            "meta": "title=\"x\"",
            "value": "meta body"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expectedEnvelope": {
        "astVersion": 1,
        "root": {
          "type": "root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "value": "meta body",
              "lang": "zzz-unknown",
              "meta": "title=\"x\""
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
